A reply's think block ends at the first `</think>` that starts a line outside a ``` fence (server/reply_text.zig).

Stock ends it at the first `</think>` anywhere. When the model reasons about chat templates or parsers it quotes the tag
inline (seen in pi: "outputs `<think>\n\n</think>\n\n`, else `<think>\n`"), and everything after the quote, the rest of
the reasoning, went to `content`, streamed and not; the tool-call parser read it too, so a call the reasoning only
mentioned could become a real one. `<think>`/`</think>` are ordinary tokens 248068/248069 here (not special), the same ids
whether quoted or real, so the split decides by position: Qwen 3.5 models close reasoning with "\n</think>\n\n". A finished
reply with no line-start closer falls back to its first `</think>` (stock); while streaming, an inline one stays reasoning.
Only the `</think>` markers change (not Gemma's channel markers). usage.reasoning_tokens still counts to the first
`</think>` token.

TENSORFOLD_THINK_LINE_CLOSE=0 restores the stock split.
Verified: Zig unit test in reply_text.zig (quoted, fenced, plain, inline, empty block, quoted call; stock tests pass);
bench/think_check.py (11 cases, streamed and not) and bench/template_check.py on the served model; README.

